codex
The first oracle run exposed a real generator flaw, not merely an easy preset: every recovered row and column pair differed by exactly 32. The affine Feistel round leaks a fixed high-bit differential, so the existing G6 “visible half shift” attack was testing the wrong offset and missed a 3/3 successful construction-aware attack. I’m fixing the permutation layer and adding that exact differential attack to the gate before spending more oracle calls.
