codex
One oracle still solved the revised easy rung by carrying out the inverse computation. That does not yet kill the family—the ladder is meant to escalate—but it confirms the difficulty is the amount of exact hand computation, not just discovery of the half-order invariant. I’m letting the other two vendors finish to see whether this rung is uniformly easy.
