codex
The first `n=20` oracle still solved correctly, so width alone is not a reliable barrier. I’m checking the other vendors, but I’m also treating this as a warning against claiming that larger labels create meaningful structural difficulty; if the full panel keeps solving, the honest outcome will be a Track B rejection or park rather than an arithmetic arms race.
