codex
Implemented and verified a native Track B generator based on [Latin trades and simplicial complexes](https://arxiv.org/abs/0907.1481).

Key results:

- Shipping preset: `medium` (`n=64`)
- Official oracle verdict: `hardened`
- Bare shipping arm: 0/3 solved
- Structural hint: 0/3 solved
- Placebo hint: 0/3 solved
- Guessing: 0/200,000; exact probability ≈ `2.94e-39`
- Five adversarial attacks: each 0/8
- Gaussian reference algorithm: 23,327 counted operations
- Compact route: 107 operations
- Answer size: 173 characters, 44 estimated tokens, 8 atoms
- Emit validation succeeded with JSON-native answers

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.1481/gen_0907_1481.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.1481/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.1481/README.md)
- [Official hardening transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.1481/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.1481/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.1481/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hardening metadata](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.1481/.meta.json)

The initial Feistel construction was discarded after a construction-aware differential attack solved it. The shipped version uses exact xorshift relabellings, even-parity intercalate switches, and composition-of-identities generation without solving generated instances.
